386→                        <div id="content">Let $\epsilon&#62;0$. Is there some set $A\subset \mathbb{N}$ of density $&#62;1-\epsilon$ such that $a_1\cdots a_r=b_1\cdots b_s$ with $a_i,b_j\in A$ can only hold when $r=s$?<br><br>Similarly, can one always find a set $A\subset\{1,\ldots,N\}$ with this property of size $\geq (1-o(1))N$?</div>
387→                        <div id="problem_id"><a href="/786">#786</a>: <a href="#cite-Er65-786" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er65','786'); return false;">[Er65]</a><a href="#cite-Er69-786" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er69','786'); return false;">[Er69,p.81]</a><a href="#cite-Er73-786" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er73','786'); return false;">[Er73,p.132]</a></div>
